sPod Firmware 0.9.1
Release date: 2026-06-09

Summary
-------
This release stabilizes the audio path, improves SD-based catalog handling,
adds Wi-Fi story upload support, and introduces release/version metadata.

Added
-----
- Firmware version is now defined as 0.9.1 in the ESP-IDF project metadata.
- Firmware logs its version at startup.
- Wi-Fi story upload flow for adding story folders and MP3 chapters from a browser.
- Browser-side cover extraction from MP3 ID3 APIC artwork during Wi-Fi upload.
- Generated upload cover is converted to a compatible baseline JPEG cover.jpg.
- Sound Enricher replaces the older loudness behavior for richer low-volume sound.
- Sound Enricher amount profiles:
  - Warm around 40%.
  - Full around 75%.
  - Punch around 100%.
- Mono downmix control and equal-power stereo-to-mono mixing.
- Playback timing diagnostics for SD read latency and I2S write timeouts.
- Release export batch file for collecting firmware artifacts.

Changed
-------
- MP3 playback decoder moved from minimp3 to Espressif esp_audio_codec simple decoder.
- MP3 stream handling now preserves unconsumed decoder input between reads.
- Sound Enricher now fades out as volume rises so it mainly affects low-volume playback.
- Loudness API remains as a compatibility stub, but loudness processing is no longer used.
- Tone controls and Sound Enricher are now separate stages in the playback path.
- Catalog cover selection now prefers explicit cover files over generated ID3COVR files.
- Existing ID3COVR files are no longer treated as explicit cover art candidates.
- Upload workflow can generate cover.jpg automatically from embedded MP3 artwork.
- MP3 playback log now reports stream sample rate, channel count, and bit depth.
- Decoder ready log now reports esp_audio_codec instead of minimp3.

Fixed
-----
- Fixed stereo-to-mono behavior that could sound like one channel was being favored.
- Fixed possible frame-boundary loss in streamed MP3 decoding.
- Reduced risk of intermittent stutter on high bitrate or VBR MP3 files.
- Avoided marking playback as finished when decoder setup fails.
- Avoided I2S output buffer underrun/corruption risk when decoded mono input is duplicated to stereo output.
- Avoided repeated use of incompatible generated ID3COVR artwork when explicit cover.jpg is available.
- Avoided progressive JPEG cover extraction crashes by moving compatibility conversion to upload time.

Functional Notes
----------------
- For best cover compatibility, use Wi-Fi upload or provide an explicit cover.jpg/cover.png in the story folder.
- Sound Enricher is intended to replace loudness. Test at low volumes first; at higher volumes it intentionally has less effect.
- This release expects esp_audio_codec to be fetched by ESP-IDF Component Manager during configure/build.
- A normal reconfigure/build should be enough after this release metadata change; full clean should only be needed if Component Manager or CMake cache gets stuck.
